{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>וָאֶתְפֹּשׂ בִּשְׁנֵי</b> etc. One needs to know why it was necessary to grasp them — were they not in his hand? And perhaps when Israel had not sinned the tablets were hovering above Moses' hand and his hand could not reach to take them, as may be inferred from the precision of the verse's saying in the preceding verse ״וּשְׁנֵי הַלֻּחֹת עַל שְׁתֵּי יָדָי״ — and it did not say ״בִּשְׁתֵּי יָדַי״ or ״בְּיָדַי,״ but rather intended to say that they were not literally in his hands but hovering above his hands, bearing themselves up; and after he saw the calf, the power of their holiness was removed and it became necessary to grasp them with his hand."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:16:21.384410931Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}